comments.body:
@yuzie007 This includes your fix from just now (optimizer restart with Path) and the windows baoab test fix I just did, as well as remaining resource warning fixes.  I didn't see anything extremely alarming on the issues list.  Are we waiting for anything else?

I realized that if the tests run from a non-editable installed ASE (e.g. using `ase test` after pip install), there's an ambiguity where pytest settings in pyproject.toml are not visible to pytest since those settings were not installed.  That produces a lot of warnings about unknown markers and other things.

We could consider *not* installing the tests, getting rid of the `ase test` command (although some people like it a lot) in the future, but of course that would be too much before release.  Alternatively one can specify warning/marker stuff in conftest, but it also doesn't feel right to have scattered pytest configuration.
